<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James II of Urgell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1380–1433</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as James the Unfortunate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James II of Urgell was count of Urgell from 1408 and a great-grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iv-of-aragon">Alfonso IV of Aragon</a>. When Martin I died without an heir in 1410 he was the leading Catalan claimant to the Crown of Aragon, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compromise-of-caspe">Compromise of Caspe</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-aragon">Ferdinand of Antequera</a> in 1412. His revolt in 1413 ended with the surrender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balaguer">Balaguer</a>, the loss of his county and imprisonment until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-urgell.jpg" alt="James II of Urgell" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Peter_II,_Count_of_Urgell.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
